recite turns text into verified speech.

Usage:
  recite [global flags] <command> [flags] [arguments]
  recite [flags] TEXT...       same as: recite say TEXT...

Commands:
  say       Text to verified audio file (default command)
  render    Render a batch or project into many outputs
  check     Text guard, spoken form and chunk plan, no network
  prepare   Write the editable spoken-form script
  voices    List voices; --preview DIR renders a sample of each
  doctor    Check the environment and the route
  auth      Login state, or sign in through codex
  usage     Local ledger summary and Codex plan status
  cache     Manage the take cache
  config    Effective merged config and its sources
  version   Version, commit, build date and Go version
  help      Show help for recite or a command

Global flags:
  -auth-source SOURCE
    	auth SOURCE: auto, codex or file (default auto)
  -codex-bin PATH
    	codex binary PATH
  -codex-home DIR
    	codex home DIR
  -config PATH
    	read config from PATH
  -debug-dir DIR
    	write debug artifacts to DIR
  -json
    	machine-readable output
  -log-file PATH
    	write the log to PATH
  -no-color
    	disable colour
  -profile NAME
    	use config profile NAME
  -q	quiet: errors only
  -quiet
    	quiet: errors only
  -v	verbose (repeatable)
  -verbose
    	verbose (repeatable)

Exit codes:
  0    Success
  1    Internal error (bug)
  2    Usage or input error: bad flag, bad input encoding, missing encoder, unknown voice
  3    Auth: not signed in, not a ChatGPT sign-in, refresh failed
  4    Route denied: the token was refused for this model or endpoint
  5    Verification failed for at least one chunk after all attempts
  6    Rate-limited or quota exhausted after backoff
  7    Network, server or protocol failure after retries
  130  Interrupted
When several failures occur, the most severe is reported: 130 > 3 > 4 > 1 > 7 > 6 > 5 > 2.

Run "recite help <command>" for a command's flags.
